00:04:13,636 --> 00:04:19,636
It ain't ogre...til it's ogre.

2
00:08:27,272 --> 00:08:33,272
Shrek Forever After is a comedy, adventure,
fantasy film directed by Mike Mitchell.

3
00:12:40,909 --> 00:12:46,909
A midlife-crisis burdened Shrek, longing for the days when he felt like a
real ogre, makes a pact with magic deal-maker Rumpelstiltskin.

4
00:16:54,545 --> 00:17:00,545
But when he's duped and sent to a twisted version of Far Far Away—where Rumpelstiltskin is king, ogres are
hunted, and he and Fiona have never met—he sets out to restore his world and reclaim his true love.

5
00:21:08,181 --> 00:21:14,181
Shrek (voice), played by Mike Myers.

6
00:25:21,818 --> 00:25:27,818
Donkey (voice), played by Eddie Murphy.

7
00:29:35,454 --> 00:29:41,454
Princess Fiona (voice), played by Cameron Diaz.

8
00:33:49,090 --> 00:33:55,090
Puss in Boots (voice), played by Antonio Banderas.

9
00:38:02,727 --> 00:38:08,727
Rumpelstiltskin / Priest / Krekraw Ogre (voice), played by Walt Dohrn.

10
00:42:16,363 --> 00:42:22,363
Queen Lillian (voice), played by Julie Andrews.

11
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Shrek Forever After is a 2010 American animated fantasy comedy film
loosely based on the 1990 children's picture book Shrek!

12
00:50:43,636 --> 00:50:49,636
by William Steig.

13
00:54:57,272 --> 00:55:03,272
Directed by Mike Mitchell, and written by Josh Klausner and Darren
Lemke, it is the fourth installment in the Shrek franchise.

14
00:59:10,909 --> 00:59:16,909
The film stars Mike Myers, Eddie Murphy, Cameron Diaz, Antonio Banderas, Julie Andrews, and John Cleese
reprising their voice roles from the previous films, with Walt Dohrn joining the cast.

15
01:03:24,545 --> 01:03:30,545
The story follows Shrek, now a domesticated family man and local celebrity, longing for his days of solitude and being
feared, leading him to make a magic deal with the deceitful imp Rumpelstiltskin, which creates grave consequences.

16
01:07:38,181 --> 01:07:44,181
Shrek Forever After premiered at the Tribeca Film Festival on April 21, 2010, and was
theatrically released by Paramount Pictures in the United States on May 21.

17
01:11:51,818 --> 01:11:57,818
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $756
million, becoming the fifth-highest-grossing film of 2010.

18
01:16:05,454 --> 01:16:11,454
Although intended to be the final film in the
series, a fifth film is in development.

19
01:20:19,090 --> 01:20:25,090
Two spin-off films, Puss in Boots (2011) and Puss in Boots: The Last Wish (2022), have also
been released, while a spin-off centered around Donkey is in development.

20
01:24:32,727 --> 01:24:38,727
The film explores themes of witch, villain, sequel, ogre.

21
01:28:46,363 --> 01:28:52,363
The tone is lighthearted and mind_bending.
